\newlabel{fig:sch-ce-npn}{{3}{6}{Common-emitter circuits for the NPN transistor: (a) input-characteristic circuit, $V_{CC}$ decade swept from 0.01 to \SI {1}{\volt } for the plotted family (the $V_{CC} = \SI {1}{\volt }$ curve is the reference for the input resistance), $R_B = \SI {10}{\kilo \ohm }$, $V_{BB}$ swept; (b) output-characteristic circuit, $V_{BB} = \SI {0}{\volt }$ (stepped to \SI {8}{\volt }), $R_B = \SI {100}{\kilo \ohm }$, $V_{CC}$ swept}{figure.caption.4}{}}
